| 0 | -0.015601 | 0.209858 | 13/64 |
| 1 | -0.889401 | 0.068355 | 6/64 |
| 2 | -0.982549 | 0.044092 | 5/64 |
| 3 | -0.987830 | 0.041948 | 7/64 |
\image(figures/simsiam_fit.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Alignment, feature spread and matching-crop retrieval on held-out view pairs.)
\alttext(Three line plots show held-out alignment loss, target spread and nearest-positive retrieval by epoch.)

The alignment loss approaches its lower bound of -1 while target spread
shrinks and nearest-positive retrieval declines. On this compact fixture,
the predictor aligns the views even as the target representation loses
information that distinguishes sources.

> Reference

- [Chen and He (2021), Exploring Simple Siamese Representation Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.10566).
